File name: SFUPGPSS.MP
Path description: Path through great pyramid, level 1 (default one doesn't work).
Path starts: Firepit under pyramid.
Path ends: Stone Sphinx level 1.
Area of the game: Module 6
Level recommendation: N/A
Type of path: Path
File format: New
Monsters encountered: unsure.
Additional information:

This path replaces the default MegaMud path through the great pyramid's first
level, as the default one doesn't work.

As a tip for people travelling through the great pyramidm take these bits
of advice from Wulfman (many thanks to him for these):


First lvl of the great pyramid, begins at firepit ends at sphinx on lvl
1 (this may require adding "ask sphinx fire" and an up depending on the
lvl 2 path you are intending to use. This path works... however, no path
is going to work in the pyramid 100% of the time. Depending on changes
in room checksums as doors are opened this path may still need some
work. It will not however cause the lockup problems or loading failure
problems of the default path.
Keep in mind that the entire pyramid is designed to mess with a script.
Get held by an undead priest or stop to rest and you will end up back in
the firepit lvl.
Things that will increase this path's probability of success will depend
upon your character class and the gear available to you.

Obstacles:
Various types of warriors, wussies... ignore them if at all possible.
Asps, light damage but long lasting poison that can really add up
Undead Priests, FEAR them.... they cast versions of hold and blind that
last forever it seems... as well as "a dark spell" that can knock 40-50
HP off you twice a round...


Tactics: Grab yourself a cooler full of soda.... a couple bags of chips
and some Ho-Ho's... disable call wasting... put something soothing on
the headphones, and nail the door shut.... OH, a really comfy chair is a
must..... prepare to camp out on this one.

if you can't sneak past these guys or run away, dispatch them as quickly
as possible, if one gets a cast of hold on you, use diamond studded ring
or cast freedom ASAP and KEEP MOVING.

If you get low on HP don't wait to die... drop carrier, you will
re-enter in the firepits, just like the crypt quest puts you out in the
front entrance to the crypt.

Gear:
cure poison potions - even if you can cast cure/anti... save your mana
for casting freedom and cure blindness.
ethereal amulet - get all the magic res you can get your paws on.
green potions - speed is of the essence... you get no special bonus for
how many monsters you kill on this lvl... take too long and you fall on
your butt in the firepits.
Diamond studded Ring only 3 in a game, not a must have but it sure helps